desc:TT-303PATGEN
// @description TT-303PATGEN - Acid pattern generator with MIDI output (TT-303 or any synth)
// @author TimTechlor
// @version 1.0.2
// @license MIT
// @tags midi acid 303 pattern generator sequencer markov euclid slide accent
// @link Manual https://timtechlor.de/docs/tt-303patgen-manual.html
// @provides
//   [nomain] img/tt-ui-options/303patgen-front.png
//   [nomain] img/tt-ui-options/303patgen-options.png
//   tt-303patgen-manual.html
//   [main] TT-303PATGEN Print to MIDI Item.lua
//   [main] TT-303PATGEN Print Song Chain.lua
//   img/tt-303patgen/tt-303patgen-gallery.png
//   img/tt-303patgen/tt-303patgen-long.png
//   img/tt-303patgen/tt-303patgen-presets.png
//   img/tt-303patgen/tt-303patgen-song.png
// @about
//   # TT-303PATGEN
//   MIDI-only acid pattern generator for REAPER. Generates 303-style
//   patterns (16 to 32 steps, note / octave / gate / tie / accent / slide /
//   probability per step) and plays them as MIDI, synced to the host
//   transport. Accent = velocity above the synth's threshold (default 127
//   vs. 64, threshold 65 as in the TT-303 1.5.0), slide = overlapping legato notes - exactly what the TT-303
//   expects in HOST mode, and what any other mono synth understands.
//   Five algorithms (random walk, Markov, Euclid, motif+variation, classic
//   mutation), ten scales plus a custom mask, seeded and reproducible,
//   mutate / rotate / reverse / invert / double, eight pattern slots (A-H),
//   song chain, 32 built-in style patterns plus 16 factory scenes, swing, humanize, MIDI transpose
//   (C2 = original pitch) and an optional gmem link (namespace tt303pg).
//   Operated from the drawn front panel; all parameters stay automatable.
// @changelog
//   1.0.2 - PRINT TO MIDI ITEM can no longer pick up a half-written pattern while the pattern is being changed (the link block is marked invalid during the rewrite and the print script reads again). Source comments cleaned up. Generator, sound of the output and saved state are unchanged.
//   1.0.1 - Robustness fixes from a code review: damaged or truncated project data no longer leaves a half-loaded state (the generator falls back to defaults), a truncated preset bank is reported as BANK DAMAGED instead of silently emptying, and a zero time-signature numerator can no longer divide by zero. Sound, generator, MIDI output and the saved format are unchanged; projects saved with 1.0.0 load as before.
//   1.0.0 - First public release (ACID SEASON Drop 01). Same code as 0.9.0: generator, MIDI output, front and saved state are unchanged, so projects and presets saved with 0.9.x load as before. Version number only.
//   0.9.0 - Fixes from a code review and a longer test run: with step locks, GENERATE / TRY / seed re-generate / REROLL ALL no longer leave a tie on the discarded note of a locked step (the tie follows the locked step); MUTATE passes a mutated note on to the ties behind it; REROLL RHYTHM keeps each step's PROB (as the other reroll modes do); the gallery's AUTO mode also re-rolls when DENS VAR changes; with HUM TIME the transposition of an incoming note is applied to a step whose humanized start falls into the next block; undo from the host resets the mutate counter like the plug-in's own UNDO; the note-transposition buffer holds up to 256 changes per block (was 30), so dense incoming MIDI at large audio buffers is transposed exactly.
//   0.8.2 - UI kit 7 inlined (shared widget library; new building blocks for text fit, knobs with value, tabs, pads, plots, scope, envelope, piano). No change to the front, the generator or the MIDI output.
//   0.8.1 - SONG tab: a running playhead in the chain timeline (bright vertical line plus a line that grows underneath it) and the playing cell is lit, so you can see where in the song the chain is. Display only; MIDI output unchanged.
//   0.8.0 - Generator and slot switching (stage 5): SLIDE % is now the share of the playing steps that slide (e.g. 20 % of 8 notes = 2 slides; the rhythm is drawn so that neighbouring notes exist - before, a slide happened with 20 % chance per neighbouring pair, 0.65 slides per pattern on average, none at all with EUCLID); EUCLID puts the first onset on step 1 and groups onsets into pairs when SLIDE is on; new DENS VAR knob spreads the number of playing steps around DENSITY; REROLL NOTES / RHYTHM / ACC+SLD are real partial modes (new tones over the existing rhythm, new rhythm over the existing tones, new accents / slides over the existing notes) built from the generator itself; SLOT QUANT (OUTPUT tab): a slot change from the front, the keys 1..8 or NOTE TRIG waits for the next beat / bar; NOTE TRIG: eight MIDI notes from TRIG BASE switch the slots A..H (they do not transpose and are not passed through). Seeds give different patterns than in 0.7.0 (saved patterns are unaffected); with NOTE TRIG off and SLOT QUANT = INSTANT the MIDI output of a pattern is unchanged.
//   0.7.0 - New workbench front (UI redesign, generator and MIDI output unchanged): all 32 steps of a pattern in one roll (VIEW FIT) with a movable pitch window and a FOCUS view (deck collapsed = the full -12..+35 range); step selection (click / drag the step numbers, Shift extends, double-click = all, Ctrl + drag in the roll) with range operations (copy / cut / paste, clear, rotate, reverse, invert, scale-degree and octave transpose, duplicate, copy to another slot, MUTATE inside the selection); SNAP (notes land on the scale, Alt inverts); 16-step undo ring across slots with REDO; MUT % slider on the front (CLASSIC MUT rate - it had no control before); "WAITING FOR AUDIO" / BUSY messages; hover keyboard (A S G T O P over a step, C X V, R I, [ ], Z / Shift+Z, Del, arrows, L - active only for the keys REAPER passes to the plug-in); deck tabs GENERATE / OUTPUT / SONG / GALLERY / LIBRARY; GALLERY: eight candidates at once (each exactly what GENERATE gives with its seed), TRY / KEEP, AUTO, partial reroll (NOTES / RHYTHM / ACC+SLD / ALL), seed history; step locks (GENERATE, MUTATE and the rerolls leave locked steps alone, saved with the project behind the preset bank); LIBRARY browser with previews; song chain editing (insert / delete / move), chain timeline, slot overview and chain length in bars; new action "TT-303PATGEN Print Song Chain" (SEQ LINK gmem block from index 200). All fixes of 0.6.2 are included. MIDI output and generator results of unchanged patterns are unchanged.
//   0.6.2 - Fixes from a second code review (all verified in REAPER): STOP / PANIC also release a sustain-on (CC 64) that is still waiting in the output queue, so no note keeps ringing when the pedal message and the stop arrive in the same block; more than 30 input notes within one block keep their exact timing for the MIDI transpose (the oldest change drops out instead of the newest value being applied too early). All fixes of 0.6.1 are included. MIDI output of unchanged patterns is unchanged.
//   0.6.1 - Fixes from the code review: STOP / PANIC release a held sustain pedal (CC 64) before the note-offs so no note keeps ringing; the output queue can no longer drop a note-off (steps are skipped instead when it is full); an input note transposes the pattern from its own timing position, not for the whole block; PRINT keeps ties as ties (a tie with a different stored pitch is no longer printed as a slide); REV keeps the probability of ties; loading a preset or scene applies rate / root / gate / ... from the new state in the same block; a second preset or scene load waits until the first one is applied; the internal UNDO button also undoes direct note / gate / accent / slide / octave / probability / length edits; factory names are built once; a note edit outside the pattern length can no longer hang the audio thread. MIDI output of unchanged patterns is unchanged.
//   0.6.0 - 16 factory scenes (S01..S16 in the FACTORY list): a scene sets a whole starting point - generator, scale / root, mutate range, rate / swing / gate / humanize, seed, slots A-D with their lengths and the song chain; slots E-H, velocities / threshold, FOLLOW, MIDI channel, RUN and SEQ LINK stay untouched. Fixes: INIT now uses NORM VEL 64 / THRESH 65 (was 90 / 100 and made every step an accent on a TT-303 >= 1.5.0); setting or dragging a note on a tie turns it into a note and the following ties follow its pitch; REV keeps ties attached to their note; FACTORY no longer adds a second undo step; pass-through MIDI (CC, pitch bend) can no longer crowd note-offs out of the output queue. Less CPU: panic skips the scan when nothing sounds, diagnostic sliders only with the test unlock (no more changing readouts in projects and presets), no library / table rebuild at transport start, FOLLOW check only on change, font fitting only for FONT sizes above 0, no double commands while painting step rows. MIDI output of the generator unchanged
//     - NEW: OPTIONS > AUTO FIT ON / OFF (default on): dragging the window edge rescales the UI to the new window size; the UI SIZE buttons still set a fixed zoom until the window changes again. UI SIZE now accepts 25 to 400 percent. Saved per instance.
//   0.5.7 - Defaults follow the TT-303 1.5.0 accent threshold (65, Devil Fish): NORM VEL 64 and THRESH 65 on a fresh instance (were 90 / 100, which made every normal step an accent on a fresh TT-303); saved projects and presets keep their values; MIDI output otherwise unchanged
//   0.5.6 - Large FONT steps: labels in tight places stay at the normal size when the larger step would not fit (no overlapping text); MIDI output unchanged
//   0.5.5 - Persistent UI size and options; larger default, stable colours when zooming.
//   0.5.4 - Fixes: HUMANIZE can no longer start a step before the previous one (a slide could leave a note hanging); two panics in one block (CC 120 + CC 123) release every note; the MIDI monitor is visible again (GENERATOR panel moved down, knobs slightly smaller); MIDI CH 16 can be chosen at the front (0 no longer possible); clicking a note in the piano roll removes it again; pattern edits are REAPER undo points (Ctrl+Z) and mark the project as changed; mouse wheel moves stepped knobs / sliders by one step per detent; GATE LEN 100 % with a rising tempo no longer overlaps notes; preset bar tooltips at the right place (suite-wide tooltip helper); test commands only with a test script unlock; ReaPack installs the manual images and lists the Print script as an action
//   0.5.3 - OPTIONS box: TOOLTIPS ON / OFF (per instance, saved with the project); tooltips on every control incl. the preset bar and the OPTIONS button, shown after a short hover (0.35 s) and not while dragging; DSP/audio unchanged
//   0.5.2 - OPTIONS box: fully clamped inside the window incl. shadow; footer no longer overlaps the colour picker; user preset bank stays loadable when the chunk was saved with fewer slots; DSP/audio unchanged
//   0.5.1 - OPTIONS box: FONT SIZE for FONT 1 (titles) and FONT 2 (text), custom HSV colour picker for FONT 1 / FONT 2 / BG with RESET / RESET ALL, live, per instance, low-contrast warning; dim text contrast raised to WCAG >= 4.5 in all 10 schemes; DSP unchanged
//   0.5.0 - Preset bar in the header (left of OPTIONS): 32 library patterns as FACTORY list, 32 user presets (generator / output
//           settings, scale / root / seed, all 8 patterns and the song chain) stored in the plug-in state (project, FX chain, REAPER preset file);
//           the old library combo + LOAD is replaced by the bar; MIDI monitor moved into the slot row
//   0.4.0 - OPTIONS box with COLOR (10 schemes), per instance (hidden slider 64)
//   0.3.0 - ReaScript "Print to MIDI Item", SEQ LINK timing extension block, PANIC button, transport-jump
//           robustness (state kept across the re-run of @init)
//   0.2.0 - Song chain, humanize (deterministic timing / velocity jitter), per-step probability, SEQ LINK sender
//           (gmem tt303pg), MIDI channel / accent threshold controls
//   0.1.0 - Core: 8 slots x 32 steps, five generator algorithms (random walk, Markov, Euclid, motif, classic
//           mutation), ten scales + custom mask, seed / lock, GENERATE + MUTATE + rotate / reverse / invert /
//           double / clear / copy / paste / undo, library of 32 style patterns, sample-accurate MIDI output with
//           swing, slide overlap, ties, accent velocity, MIDI transpose (C2 = original), panic handling,
//           piano-roll front panel
// History (P25): @changelog sorted by version (now 0.5.3, 0.5.2, 0.1.0 .. 0.5.1); @provides extended by the six manual images
// and [main] for the print script (previously ReaPack did not install the images and did not register the script as an action).
// Spec: ../auftraege/P11_TT-303PATGEN.md (+ _ERGAENZUNG_gegenlesung.md)
// Sliders = data channel (all hidden with '-'); operation only through the @gfx front.
// Patterns and slots live in JSFX memory and in @serialize (serVer PG_SER).

options:gmem=tt303pg

